
=== live mode: the sentence translated as it is typed ===
  ok   ships a debounce shorter than the menu's and no word floor
  ok   turns on with the binding's prompt and says so, changing no menu setting
  ok   sends the sentence to translate_en after the live debounce, not the menu's
  ok   sends at once when a word ends, without waiting for the live debounce (live-word-end-instant)
  ok   keeps the live debounce at a word end once the instant word end is switched off (live-word-end-instant)
  ok   a live keystroke is automatic: it still waits for the backend's interval (explicit-never-held)
  ok   asks from the first word, below the menu's minimum word count
  ok   runs with the menu's count when the binding names none
  ok   ignores the answer of a request a new keystroke superseded
  ok   does not ask again about the accepted sentence until the user types

=== live mode: turning it on and off ===
  ok   a second press turns it off, whatever its prompt, and typing is the menu's again
  ok   turning off withdraws the live offer on screen
  ok   refuses a prompt that no longer exists, and stays off
  ok   stops, never falls back, when its prompt is deleted while it runs
  ok   refuses an invalid parameter without turning on
  ok   refuses like a manual prediction while the AI is off, paused or has no backend
  ok   a pause turns it off silently, and resuming leaves it off
  ok   switching the AI off turns it off silently
  ok   is off at every start

=== live mode: hotstrings, Tab and explicit actions ===
  ok   waits while a hotstring preview is shown, then asks once it is gone
  ok   an expansion dismisses the live tooltip and asks again about the expanded text
  ok   leaves Tab alone without a live tooltip on screen
  ok   an explicit action takes over, and live mode resumes at the next keystroke

=== live mode: one normal profile chooser and retained prompt actions ===
  ok   has one profile chooser, keeps prompt actions and retires their override on explicit selection

=== live mode: the daemon tells the engine ===
  ok   forwards every pause transition and redraws the tray on a live change

=== manual profile selection retires retained Linux live actions ===
  ok   requires exact stop ACK before profile persistence and never redraws a refused cancellation
  ok   retains the real shortcut stop notice in all locales while the second chooser stays absent
  ok   retains a free-language live receipt through the actual typing timer
